# Errors & Observability

## Purpose

Turn backend failures into safe, consistent user-facing messages — no silent swallowing.

## When Applied

Writing repository calls, BLoC error handling, or UI error surfaces.

## Requirements

- Map `PostgrestException` (and Supabase auth/storage errors) to a user-facing `Exception`/`String` in the data layer, like existing repos.
- BLoCs emit an explicit error state; UI shows it via `custom_snackbar` or an error widget.
- Never `catch` and discard; at minimum log and rethrow a typed/user-safe message.
- Do not leak raw Postgres/RLS messages to end users.

## Examples

```dart
try {
  await _client.rpc('verify_payment', params: {...});
} on PostgrestException catch (e) {
  throw Exception(_friendly(e)); // mapped, user-safe
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- `catch (_) {}` empty blocks that hide failures.
- Surfacing `PostgrestException.message` (may reveal schema/RLS) directly in UI.

## Common Mistakes

- Handling errors in the widget instead of the BLoC state.
- Losing the original cause when rethrowing.
